              <li><strong>Orientation Auto-Detection:</strong> Portrait photos automatically generate portrait PDF pages, while wide panoramic landscapes create landscape pages.</li>
              <li><strong>High-DPI Support:</strong> Supports 300 DPI print-ready specifications without downscaling.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 5: Real-World Use Cases -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Common Use Cases for Converting Images to PDF
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          {[
            { icon: '💼', title: 'Business Expense Reports', desc: 'Photograph physical paper receipts on your smartphone, merge them into a single PDF, and submit them directly for company reimbursement.' },
            { icon: '🎓', title: 'Student Assignment Submissions', desc: 'Snap photos of handwritten mathematics homework or research diagrams and compile them into one orderly assignment file for your professor.' },
            { icon: '🏦', title: 'Banking & Loan Applications', desc: 'Assemble photos of your government ID card, salary slips, and utility bills into a single encrypted-ready PDF for banking KYC verification.' },
            { icon: '🎨', title: 'Graphic Design Portfolios', desc: 'Combine individual PNG render exports, branding mockups, and client proofs into an attractive multi-page portfolio presentation.' },
            { icon: '📦', title: 'Ecommerce Product Catalogues', desc: 'Merge product inventory photos with specifications to send wholesale buyer lookbooks and spec sheets via email or WhatsApp.' },
